will list the last login session of specified or for all users by
default.   Each  line  of  output contains the user name, the tty
from which the session was conducted, any hostname, and the start
time for the session.  If multiple are given, the session  infor‐
mation for each user is printed in the order given on the command
line.  Otherwise, information for all users is printed, sorted by
uid.   differs  from in that it only prints information regarding
the very last login session.  The last login  database  is  never
turned  over or deleted in standard usage.  The following options
are available: Use fixed widths for all output  fields.   Process
